    {
     "ord": 3,
     "period": {
      "start": "1926-01-01",
      "end": "1939-09-20"
     },
     "periodStartPrecision": "year",
     "periodEndPrecision": "day",
     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "師長與 Kraków 集團軍司令",
      "en": "Division command and Army Kraków"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "1926至1928年他任第23步兵師步兵指揮官，1928至1937年任第8步兵師師長；1929年晉升准將。1937年5月起任總監察長下的特派將領，1939年3月23日起出任 Kraków 集團軍司令。美軍戰史稱其被配屬七個步兵師與一個騎兵旅。IPN 另稱，9月2日該集團軍部隊被迫撤出西里西亞築壘區，杜納耶茨防線隨後被突破。9月20日起他成為德軍戰俘。",
      "en": "In 1926–1928 he was infantry commander of the 23rd Infantry Division and in 1928–1937 commanded the 8th Infantry Division; he became brigadier general in 1929. From May 1937 he was a general for special tasks with the Inspector General of the Armed Forces, and from 23 March 1939 commanded Army Kraków. A US Army history says he was assigned seven infantry divisions and a cavalry brigade. IPN adds that on 2 September the army's units were forced out of the Silesian fortified area and that the Dunajec line was later broken. From 20 September he was a German prisoner."
     },
